✔ JavaScript is limited to the service worker, release shims and exact reviewed tooling (35.304626ms)
✔ the two release shims only point at the TypeScript they stand for (0.611429ms)
✔ every file in public/ is an asset the release package admits (no dot-file, no map, no manifest, no xml) (15.416625ms)
✔ the Worker config is the one the release package fixes, and the Worker exports its Durable Object (1.388143ms)
✔ the default build config emits no source map (maps are opt-in, SOURCEMAPS=1, into dist-maps/) (0.400541ms)
✔ a new device sees five steps and starts on the first; a settling life has no "Who are you?" (1.760603ms)
✔ what blocks a step, in words (0.287988ms)
✔ the stage looks close at hair and faces, at the outfit for clothes; undo keeps a bounded history of real changes (0.908315ms)
✔ a skipped spirit step still holds two different traits and a dream (0.39214ms)
✔ the settle plan sends only what the server does not hold, in order, and the home last (0.458189ms)
✔ places are data: the open city is found, the others are coming and have no local governments to choose (5.509194ms)
✔ the starter wardrobe leaves out what only the Boutique sells; the rest of the editor locks the same way (1.501285ms)
✔ putting on an accessory replaces the one in its slot; at the limit the oldest gives way; tapping again takes it off (1.833564ms)
✔ choosing a colour sets the field; choosing a body keeps the style when the new body has it and falls back to one that is owned (0.361945ms)
✔ where the preview looks: the open tab, then what was changed last, then the stage's own switch (0.546296ms)
✔ the words of a look: summary, text alternative and what the scene is given (0.828746ms)
✔ the same look is the same whatever order the accessories are in and however the optional fields are spelled (0.302909ms)
✔ a random look is one a new Sim may wear, and the server would accept it (3.545841ms)
✔ the flat figure: a shadow first, the face in the middle, a hoodie drawn with its hood, a gele in front (1.009229ms)
✔ a life is held at the landing screen until its look is confirmed - unless its Play is on its way (0.301573ms)
✔ Play checks the name first, then that the character is one a new Sim may wear; the name is trimmed (0.622804ms)
✔ the server's refusal wins over the sheet's own sentence; the link note stays quiet while there is something more important (0.468625ms)
✔ a guest starts on the second card; a life that was never a guest starts on the look (0.088018ms)
✔ the look kept on the device is used only while every part of it is still a valid free choice, and only for its owner (0.65105ms)
✔ why the sheet opened is said once, in the words of the existing sheet, and only to a guest (13.881419ms)
✔ the primary action of each card says what it does and what is still missing (0.356892ms)
✔ moving in sends the chosen local government and how it was found - nothing when none was chosen - and "stay" when asked (0.159991ms)
✔ a guest who has earned something keeps it: the start cash tops the wallet up (0.234302ms)
✔ a third trait swaps out the first; a picked trait is put back by a second tap (0.23061ms)
✔ a refused step says why: offline in the connection's own words, otherwise the server's sentence (0.166501ms)
✔ the session form sends the nickname trimmed (0.084543ms)
✔ a refused name is put in the draft once; after that the field follows the draft (Shuffle and the dice are not dead) (0.233553ms)
✔ fresh nickname entry is mandatory only until connection; expired saved previews stay dismissible (0.109102ms)
✔ a full world: the wait before the start is sent again grows to a minute and is spread, and the screen says nothing is lost (0.258405ms)
✔ too many new players from one network: the screen says it is the network, how long to wait, and that nothing is lost (0.199846ms)
✔ deployed Nigeria tiers match pinned bytes and fit their host reservations including shadows (9.742807ms)
✔ Lagos revision preserves accepted navigation and binds its published manifest (1.556824ms)
✔ actual Lagos host markers cannot disconnect the authored sidewalk or action anchors (99.957473ms)
✔ rectangle complement preserves overlapping corridors and clips outside rectangles (17.499664ms)
✔ all batch001 anchors are reachable exactly from supported entrance without clearing blockers (30.20642ms)
✔ Lagos excludes near furniture for both tiers and corrects elevated sidewalk/entrance (0.331668ms)
✔ Abuja rejects unsupported north strip and preserves raised median crossing (0.989655ms)
✔ host rejection retries on ambient guards with cooldown and a finite per-tier limit (21.518995ms)
✔ transient rejection recovers with refreshed actor budgets and near/far admission (7.847686ms)
✔ late hero eviction clears selection, waits for capacity and recovers without repeated downloads (20.633614ms)
✔ stale tier completion and disposal cannot poison the new selection or retain geometry (11.746999ms)
✔ scene teardown cannot rebuild contact or ambient state through disposal callbacks (11.942285ms)
✔ late parsing after scene teardown releases resources without host callbacks (16.065129ms)
✔ runtime PBR keeps authored material and shares one transform with every navigation shape (7.848718ms)
✔ indoors forces near and changing tiers releases materials, textures and shared images exactly once (4.904983ms)
✔ cancelled parsing is serialized, disposed and never attached after a newer selection or scene teardown (5.269906ms)
✔ over-budget, light-bearing and failed modules leave no resident and allow retry (4.204495ms)
✔ invalid navigation is rejected before network access (1.966123ms)
✔ network loader rejects altered bytes and external resources before parsing (32.920138ms)
✔ quarter-turn collision contract and explicit shadow-pass allowance fail closed (1.705949ms)
✔ far requests close to the module still use near geometry (0.920884ms)
✔ repeated geometry groups reserve each double-sided transparent pass (1.472702ms)
✔ GPU residency counts sampler and colour-space variants of one decoded image (4.530234ms)
✔ module-owned shadow materials isolate texture lifetimes and dispose grouped maps exactly once (1.12583ms)
✔ parametric identity keeps each venue kind semantic, reachable and inside the scene budget (368.693119ms)
✔ all roof, sign, prop and landmark options build, while an absent design keeps the legacy path (541.772186ms)
✔ parametric worship is neutral only without an explicit authored variant (86.391817ms)
✔ every generated base kind stays within budget with every design and a full crowd (3794.818048ms)
✔ flat venue contact follows the rendered ground top and refuses unsupported or mismatched samples (186.207831ms)
✔ declared decks must agree with their rendered solid top (292.053353ms)
✔ declared ramps and released scenes never retain contact support (146.238026ms)
✔ host lights dispose owned shadow targets once and preserve unrelated lights (allocated=false) (3.438749ms)
✔ host lights dispose owned shadow targets once and preserve unrelated lights (allocated=true) (1.388108ms)
✔ actual host teardown releases shadow targets before renderer teardown (540.312107ms)
✔ large venue shadow coverage preserves sunlight direction and resets after travel (1.600862ms)
✔ idle venue performs zero renders; each change draws exactly one frame (1506.068946ms)
✔ an idle venue with a crowd renders zero frames; the crowd, the player and the lighting each cost one frame when they change (366.889394ms)
✔ leaving a venue disposes its scene; home shows the player’s avatar and guests under its clock lighting (476.262127ms)
✔ a supplied scene without a lighting preset restores host defaults after an outdoor venue (155.245786ms)
✔ HUD insets re-centre the scene with one frame per change, never by themselves, and keep name tags on the canvas (132.694577ms)
✔ only the motion loop and its gate (frame-gate.ts) may name a frame callback; no scene, map or shell source holds an interval (808.299587ms)
✔ RELEASE GATE: idle → zero frames; walking → frames; after arrival → flat again; tab hidden → the loop stops (1871.374041ms)
✔ camera: drag eases and stops; zoom keys and wheel dolly towards the avatar; recentre restores; keys elsewhere do nothing (50.328146ms)
✔ arrows and W A S D walk in the camera’s frame; walls and furniture stop the avatar; Shift jogs (115.397733ms)
✔ spots and walking stay coherent: taps walk first, the panel walks instead of teleporting, dwell selects once, activities lock (4428.746855ms)
✔ walking moves transforms only: hundreds of frames of walking, turning and zooming build no geometry (71.684005ms)
✔ arriving from above (the end of the map's dive): the camera starts high and comes down to the composed view, then the loop stops (37.772526ms)
✔ reduced motion snaps: a tap puts the avatar there in one frame and the camera never eases (31.471421ms)
✔ home: furniture is solid, a tap on the floor walks there, and Buy mode keeps its own taps (59.196932ms)
✔ EVERY VENUE: spawn on free floor, walk to every spot and back out, orbit all the way round, zoom to both limits — and the loop always stops (1534.991596ms)
✔ raised spots: the avatar climbs the declared way up, stands at the deck’s height, and a walking key takes the same way down first (49.964905ms)
✔ in sight: zoomed in behind a tree the camera is held in or the tree is ghosted — eased, then at rest; the wide view is never pulled (175.269848ms)
✔ other players stand where they report, ease when they move (bounded frames, then idle), and are simply there with reduced motion (62.883412ms)
✔ markers and people: a click on a marker’s ring picks the marker even with someone in front of it; hovering names what a click would pick (62.439613ms)
✔ where the avatar stands is reported in presence units, on request and while walking; walkBy is the keyboard way to move (33.527226ms)
✔ game tables can be walked up to: a tap walks there and opens it on arrival, resting beside one opens it once, and it costs no idle frame (3443.427126ms)
